 "booster": {
  "name": "Play Booster",
  "description": "14 cards: 5 commons, a common (a Special Guests card instead in 1 in 55 boosters), 3 uncommons, a wildcard of any rarity (a common 39.1%, an uncommon 39.1%, a rare 19.5% or a mythic rare 1.9%, or a borderless Elder Dragon, planeswalker or dual land or a field notes card), a rare (82.5%) or mythic rare (14.1%) or a borderless Elder Dragon, planeswalker or dual land (1.6%) or a field notes rare (1.2%) or mythic rare, a Mystical Archive card (an uncommon 87.5%, a rare 9.6% or a mythic rare 2.9%), a traditional foil of any rarity (a common 54.4%, an uncommon 33.6%, a rare 6.7%, a mythic rare 1.1%, a Mystical Archive uncommon 2.8%, or a Mystical Archive rare or mythic rare, a borderless Elder Dragon, planeswalker or dual land or a field notes card), and a land (a basic 26.7%, foil 6.7%; a full-art spellcraft land 13.3%, foil 3.3%; a common dual land 40%, foil 10%). Published only as less than 1%, so derived: the field notes mythic rare in the rare slot is the 0.6% left to 100%; the wildcard's borderless and field notes cards share the 0.4% left to 100% (0.19% and 0.21%, as their shares of the rare slot), the foil's Mystical Archive rares and mythic rares take the Mystical Archive slot's proportions of its 2.8% uncommons (0.31% and 0.09%) and its borderless and field notes cards share the rest of the 1.4% left (0.47% and 0.53%). Within the borderless cards a rare is twice as likely as a mythic rare, and within the field notes cards a mythic rare is half as likely as a rare, as in the Collector Booster's published odds. The Mystical Archive cards are the set's English printings (the Japanese printings come in Japanese boosters). Each booster also holds a punch-out counter card or a double-sided token, which aren't game cards.",
